      "message": "[error] Line 97: 🔴 `progress` now writes into `playback.value` (`@Published`) in `didSet`, but `progress` is fed by Rx player callbacks that are not guaranteed to run on the main thread. Publishing SwiftUI state off-main can trigger runtime warnings and flaky UI updates. Fix by ensuring all `progress` mutations (or at least `playback.value` assignment) happen on the main thread, e.g. `observe(on: MainScheduler.instance)` before setting `progress`, or dispatch/annotate with `@MainActor`.",
